    <!--
        Source-based Metadata API deploy, built as a companion to the outbound
        Change Set "20260825v3 - CustomerHub - Preferences and Payment".

        CORRECTION 2026-08-25: an earlier version of this file also included
        Network/CustomSite/DigitalExperienceConfig/ExperienceBundle, on the theory
        that deploying CustomSite from source (which never carried a `serverIsDown`
        field) would sidestep the Change Set's "no StaticResource named
        SNA_8300e_sf_default_cdn_Customer_Hub1 found" error. A dry run against acc
        disproved this: those four components are circularly dependent (Network
        needs the CustomSite, CustomSite needs the Network, DigitalExperienceConfig
        needs the ExperienceBundle) and none can be created by ANY metadata deploy
        - source or Change Set - into an org with no site at all. They are
        deliberately EXCLUDED from this package. The only fix for them is the
        manual Setup > Digital Experiences > New step in each target org
        (confirmed absent from both acc and prod as of 2026-08-24/25); deploy this
        package's content on top only after that site exists.

        Field/object scope below was derived by diffing dev's schema against acc
        AND prod independently (not assumed identical) for every object this
        feature touches, then intersecting against fields actually referenced by
        the in-scope Apex/Flow source - not hand-copied from the manifest, which
        was proven incomplete by that diff (11 more Payment__c fields, 1 more
        Contact field, and the entire BrandThemeConfig__mdt custom metadata type
        were all missing from acc/prod and unlisted).

        RESOLVED 2026-08-25 - both "zombie field" references (a field that doesn't
        exist ANYWHERE, not even dev, but a currently-Active compiled Apex class
        still referenced it from before the field was deleted) were removed at
        the code level rather than recreated as unproven fields, per explicit
        direction:
          1. Payment__c.Mail_Sent_Date__c - confirmed genuinely unused: the D+2/D+4/D+6
             reminder cadence in rab_Payment_Direct_Debit_Escalation runs off the
             flow's own RecordTriggerEvent scheduled-path offset, not a stored date
             field. Removed the dead line from Test_Svc_StripeEventProcessor and
             deleted the orphaned local field-meta.xml. Verified: 7/7 tests pass in dev.
          2. Account.PrimaryBrand__c - confirmed genuinely unused (only reference in
             the whole org was Ctrl_PreferenceCenter itself). Removed the brand-
             resolution code path built on it (Case/Contact/User branches, the
             resolveAccountContext SOQL and its PrimaryBrand__c select/filter, the
             AccountContext wrapper, PreferencePageData.primaryBrand, and the two
             dead LWC fallbacks in preferenceCenter.js) while preserving the Partner
             Network category-visibility logic, which depends only on RecordType +
             Roles, not this field. Verified: 18/18 tests pass in dev across
             Ctrl_PreferenceCenter, Ctrl_PreferenceCenterGuest, Svc_MCBrandCenter.
    -->
